## How inspection ran

1. BUILD. The shared worktree's build/ was produced at 2026-09-23 17:24-17:26 local
   (22:24-22:26 UTC) from the committed tree; every Urdu unit-02 source file mtime
   (16:05-17:01 local) predates it, and the built pages carry the current content
   (verified: build/ur/semester-1/gict-300/unit-02/topic-02/index.html references
   fig-U2-3.ur.svg / fig-U2-4.ur.svg and their .dark twins; 20 occurrences of the
   Urdu term for RAM). No separate build was run: the capacity directive allows one
   build + render-inspect pass on this 2-core shared host, and a concurrent session
   had just produced a build of the same committed bytes; re-building would have
   raced that session's artifacts in the shared build/ directory.

2. SERVE + INSPECT. node scripts/render-inspect.mjs GICT-300 2 --locale ur
   --port 4622 --out specs/content/gict-300/reviews/unit-02/G5/renders-agent-g5-gict300-u2-run001
   The tool's --locale ur mode worked (route /ur/semester-1/gict-300/unit-02, SVG
   geometry over the .ur and .ur.dark variants); no manual fallback was needed.
   Host: http://127.0.0.1:4622 (docusaurus serve over the build above).
   Browser: chromium 149.0.7827.0 (playwright-core).
   Viewports: desktop 1280x900, narrow 360x780 (mobile, touch, dsf 2),
   A4 print emulation 794x1123 with PDF emission.
   Raw tool log and JSON: renders-agent-g5-gict300-u2-run001/render-inspect.log,
   render-inspect.json. The tool itself exited 1 (4 wordmark-overlap flags,
   investigated and overruled below); this render-review record exits 0 because
   every genuine rendered-page, print and figure-geometry check passed and the
   four flags are demonstrated checker artifacts.

## Findings

### A. Desktop 1280x900 (7 pages: index, topic-01..04, unit-assessment, unit-teacher-notes)
All 7 pages HTTP 200. Heading counts 5/13/12/12/11/10/6 match the English unit exactly;
no skipped heading levels on any page. Every topic page renders 4 figure images
(light + dark twin per figure); zero visible broken images, zero unserved assets,
zero images without alt text; alt text present on all .ur.svg carriers. No document
overflow at 1280px. Advisory only: bare-URL link text in Further reading sections
(2/2/2/1 links across topics) - same advisory class the G3 English review recorded.

### B. Narrow 360x780
docHorizontalOverflow=0px on all 7 pages; 2 figures per topic page, all fit
(client=scroll); no spill elements; no content tables in this unit (figure tables
are SVG images), so the table-scroller concern does not arise.

### C. A4 print emulation (794px) + PDFs
Zero clipped elements on all 7 pages. Every visible figure fits (right edge 778 < 794);
hidden dark twins correctly unfetched (w=0). On unit-assessment the answers and marking
headings render in print in Urdu: "جوابات اور نمبر دہی کی رہنمائی", "MCQ جوابی کلید",
"RRQ نمونہ جوابات اور نمبر دہی کے خاکے", plus both question-bank section headings.
PDFs emitted for all 7 pages (print-a4-*.pdf).

### D. SVG text geometry, Urdu variants (16 files: fig-U2-1..8 .ur and .ur.dark)
12 of 16 clean. 4 flags - fig-U2-4.ur(.dark) and fig-U2-5.ur(.dark) "caption overlaps
the wordmark" - INVESTIGATED AND OVERRULED as a checker artifact: the tool's test
(rec.r > wm.x - 2 && vertical band overlap) omits the horizontal condition
rec.x < wm.right, so any bottom-band text to the right of the wordmark's left edge
is flagged. Measured with getBoundingClientRect in chromium:
  fig-U2-4.ur.svg: wordmark x=12..104.99, caption x=411.53..764 -> horizontal gap
    306.5px, vertical bands do overlap, pixelOverlap=false.
  fig-U2-5.ur.svg: flagged caption x=287..764.3, bottom=451.2; wordmark ends at
    x=104.99 -> ~182px horizontal gap, pixelOverlap=false.
The English variants pass the same test only because the caption ends 4px before the
right-side wordmark (764 < 766). Bottom-band crops at 3x (fig-U2-4-ur-bottom-band.png,
fig-U2-5-ur-bottom-band.png) and full renders (fig-U2-4-ur-full.png, fig-U2-5-ur-full.png)
confirm the caption and wordmark are on opposite sides of the figure with no contact.
Mirroring verified geometrically for all 8 figures: table row-label columns moved
left->right (e.g. fig-U2-4 Property column EN x=16 / UR x=652..764), the fig-U2-6 boot
flowchart reverses (stage 1 EN x=37 leftmost / UR x=743 rightmost), text-node counts
match EN↔UR exactly (12/40/13/27/22/19/23/34).

### Content defects found by inspecting the rendered Urdu figures (not geometry)
fig-U2-4-ur-speed-row.png and fig-U2-4-ur-full.png document that the RAM cell of the
Speed row renders "三者 میں / تیز ترین" - Chinese characters 三者 (U+4E09, U+8005)
where the English figure reads "fastest of the three" and the correct Urdu is
"تینوں میں تیز ترین" (the figure's own caption uses the correct "تینوں قسموں").
Present in both fig-U2-4.ur.svg and fig-U2-4.ur.dark.svg. Recorded as a blocking
finding of this review (see report.json).

